# Photography in progress — not published until the full set is complete.
# Anything under public/ ships on the very next deploy, so these stay out of the
# repo entirely rather than relying on nobody running `git add .`. To publish the
# set, delete the public/images/cocktails line and commit the finished images.
/photos/
/_to_delete/

# Recipe renders stay out until all 18 are shot — with one exception, the og
# cards. Every page's link preview depends on one, and all 18 are correct to
# ship today: a photograph for the 8 that are shot, a generated typographic
# card for the 10 that are not (scripts/generate-og-images.mjs).
#
# The trailing /* matters. Git never descends into an excluded *directory*, so
# a negation inside `/public/images/cocktails/` could not re-include anything.
# Excluding the contents instead leaves the directory readable, and the
# negation works. This is an allow-list: -card, -card-760, full renders, webp
# and anything added later stay ignored unless a rule names them.
/public/images/cocktails/*
!/public/images/cocktails/*-og.jpg
# Raw camera drops that landed in public/ unprocessed.
/public/images/IMG_*.jpg
/public/images/IMG_*.jpeg

# Python bytecode from scripts/photos/
__pycache__/

# The owner's home address is the CAN-SPAM footer value for the Cold Open
# republish. It belongs in the email footer and nowhere else, and this
# repository is public — so the prompt that carries it stays out of git.
claude/cc-prompt-2026-08-23-send.md

# NOTE: /social/ is deliberately NOT ignored. The rules above exist because
# anything under public/ ships on the next deploy; social/ sits outside
# public/ and cannot deploy, and unlike the recipe set these images are
# finished work with no second copy. Do not "tidy up" by adding it here.
